value.markdown:
### Minimal Setup

The only required property is `data` — a DAO. `DAOControllerConfig` is auto-created from the DAO's `of` class:

```javascript
// Minimal — config auto-derived from DAO
tag({ class: 'foam.comics.v3.DAOController', data: myDAO })

// With explicit config
tag({
  class: 'foam.comics.v3.DAOController',
  data: myDAO,
  config: foam.comics.v2.DAOControllerConfig.create({
    browseTitle: 'My Records',
    tableColumns: ['name', 'email']
  })
})
```

In the example below, `globalThis.comicsV3DemoDAO` is a seeded in-memory EasyDAO set up by the hidden script block above. Click a row to open its DetailView, or use the Create button to add a record.

value.code:
// Minimal DAOController — just a DAO, no extra config
start('div').style({ height: '500px', position: 'relative', overflow: 'hidden' })
  .tag({ class: 'foam.comics.v3.DAOController', data: globalThis.comicsV3DemoDAO })
.end();

// Custom tableColumns, browseTitle, and searchMode
start('div').style({ height: '500px', position: 'relative', overflow: 'hidden' })
  .tag({
    class: 'foam.comics.v3.DAOController',
data: globalThis.comicsV3DemoDAO,
of: 'foam.u2.demos.DemoContact',
    config: {
dao: globalThis.comicsV3DemoDAO,
      browseTitle: 'My Contacts',
      tableColumns: ['name', 'contactType', 'active'],
      searchColumns: ['name', 'email']
    }
  })
.end();

value.markdown:
### CRUD Predicates

Five predicate properties control button visibility and availability. Each is a `foam.mlang.predicate.Predicate` that evaluates against the current record (or returns a constant).

| Property | Default | Controls |
|----------|---------|----------|
| `createPredicate` | `True` | CREATE button in browse view |
| `editPredicate` | `True` | EDIT button in detail view |
| `deletePredicate` | `True` | DELETE option in detail view overflow menu |
| `copyPredicate` | `createPredicate` | COPY option in detail view overflow menu |
| `refreshPredicate` | `True` | REFRESH button in browse view |

```javascript
// Disable delete entirely:
config.deletePredicate = foam.mlang.predicate.False.create();

// Disable edit for inactive records:
config.editPredicate = foam.mlang.predicate.EqExpr.create({
  arg1: { class: '__Property__', forClass_: 'foam.u2.demos.DemoContact', name: 'active' },
  arg2: { class: 'foam.mlang.Constant', value: true }
});
```

In the example below, delete is disabled and edit is only available for active contacts (try clicking an inactive one like Carol White).

value.code:
var DC = foam.u2.demos.DemoContact;
var editActiveOnly = foam.mlang.predicate.Eq.create({
  arg1: { class: '__Property__', forClass_: 'foam.u2.demos.DemoContact', name: 'active' },
  arg2: { class: 'foam.mlang.Constant', value: true }
});
start('div').style({ height: '500px', position: 'relative', overflow: 'hidden' })
  .tag({
    class: 'foam.comics.v3.DAOController',
data: globalThis.comicsV3DemoDAO,
    config: {
dao: globalThis.comicsV3DemoDAO,
      // DELETE is disabled entirely (no delete option in overflow menu)
      deletePredicate: foam.mlang.predicate.False.create(),
      // EDIT only available for active: true records
      editPredicate: editActiveOnly
    }
  })
.end();

value.markdown:
### Canned Queries

Canned queries appear as filter tabs above the browse table. They are pre-defined predicates that users can switch between with one click.

Declare them on the model using the `CannedQuery` axiom:

```javascript
foam.CLASS({
  name: 'MyModel',
  axioms: [
    foam.comics.v2.CannedQuery.create({
      label: 'Active',
      predicateFactory: function(e) {
        return e.EQ(MyModel.ACTIVE, true);
      }
    })
  ]
});
```

Or override them per-view on the config:

```javascript
config.cannedQueries = [
  foam.comics.v2.CannedQuery.create({
    label: 'Business',
    predicateFactory: function(e) {
      return e.EQ(foam.u2.demos.DemoContact.CONTACT_TYPE, 'BUSINESS');
    }
  })
];
```

value.code:
var DC = foam.u2.demos.DemoContact;
start('div').style({ height: '500px', position: 'relative', overflow: 'hidden' })
  .tag({
    class: 'foam.comics.v3.DAOController',
data: globalThis.comicsV3DemoDAO,
    config: {
dao: globalThis.comicsV3DemoDAO,
      cannedQueries: [
        foam.comics.v2.CannedQuery.create({
          label: 'Active',
          predicateFactory: function(e) {
            return e.EQ(DC.ACTIVE, true);
          }
        }),
        foam.comics.v2.CannedQuery.create({
          label: 'Business',
          predicateFactory: function(e) {
            return e.EQ(DC.CONTACT_TYPE, 'BUSINESS');
          }
        })
      ]
    }
  })
.end();

value.markdown:
### Custom Detail and Create Views

`config.detailView` and `config.createView` are `ViewSpec` properties — any view that accepts `data` works.

```javascript
// Default detail view — tabs per section:
detailView: { class: 'foam.u2.detail.TabbedDetailView', hideActions: true }

// All sections as cards in a responsive grid:
detailView: { class: 'foam.u2.detail.SectionedDetailView' }

// Flat vertical layout — sections stacked without cards:
detailView: { class: 'foam.u2.detail.VerticalDetailView' }

// Only show specific sections:
detailView: {
  class: 'foam.u2.detail.SectionedDetailView',
  useSections: ['identity', 'preferences']
}
```

See the **SectionedDetailView** demo for deeper documentation on these views.

#### Other Config Options

- **`selectMode`**: Set `true` to enable multi-row checkbox selection (for M2M relationship pickers)
- **`CRUDEnabledActionsAuth`**: Permission-based CRUD — ties create/edit/delete/copy buttons to auth permissions
- **`click`**: Override the row-click handler — receives `(obj, id)` and can push any view

