value.markdown:
### Using DetailView Standalone

DetailView is normally used inside `DAOController`, but you can render it directly. You need:
1. `data` — the object to display (pre-loaded)
2. `config` — a `DAOControllerConfig` with a `dao` pointing to the DAO (needed for SAVE/DELETE)

```javascript
var dao = myDAO;
dao.find(recordId).then(function(rec) {
  start('div').style({ height: '600px' })
    .tag({
      class: 'foam.comics.v3.DetailView',
      data: rec,
      config: foam.comics.v2.DAOControllerConfig.create({ dao: dao })
    })
  .end();
});
```

**Note:** Without a `DAOController` parent providing the `daoController` context, DELETE will not navigate back to a list. Use `DAOController` in real apps.

value.code:
var dao = globalThis.comicsV3DetailDAO;
// Find first record and render DetailView for it
dao.skip(0).limit(1).select().then(function(sink) {
  var rec = sink.array[0];
  start('div').style({ height: '600px', position: 'relative', overflow: 'hidden' })
    .tag({
      class: 'foam.comics.v3.DetailView',
      data: rec,
      config: foam.comics.v2.DAOControllerConfig.create({ dao: dao })
    })
  .end();
});

value.markdown:
### Customising the Form (viewView)

`viewView` is the form component rendered inside DetailView. It defaults to `config.detailView`, which itself defaults to `TabbedDetailView` with `hideActions: true`.

Common options:

```javascript
// Default — one tab per section:
viewView: { class: 'foam.u2.detail.TabbedDetailView', hideActions: true }

// All sections as cards in a responsive grid:
viewView: { class: 'foam.u2.detail.SectionedDetailView' }

// Flat vertical layout — no section cards:
viewView: { class: 'foam.u2.detail.VerticalDetailView' }

// Tabular (row-per-property) layout for a specific section:
viewView: {
  class: 'foam.u2.detail.TabbedDetailView',
  sections: [{
    name: 'identity',
    view: { class: 'foam.u2.detail.TabularSectionView' }
  }]
}
```

In practice, set `config.detailView` to apply globally across `DAOController`, or set `viewView` directly on a standalone `DetailView`.

See the **SectionedDetailView** demo for deeper documentation on these form layouts.

value.code:
// Compare TabbedDetailView (default) vs SectionedDetailView
// Both are wired to the same record — changes in one update the other
var dao = globalThis.comicsV3DetailDAO;
dao.skip(0).limit(1).select().then(function(sink) {
  var rec = sink.array[0];
  var config = foam.comics.v2.DAOControllerConfig.create({ dao: dao });
  start('div').style({ display: 'flex', gap: '1rem', height: '650px' })
    .start('div').style({ flex: 1, position: 'relative', overflow: 'hidden' })
      .start('p').addClass('p-semiBold').add('TabbedDetailView (default)').end()
      .tag({
        class: 'foam.comics.v3.DetailView',
        data: rec,
        config: config,
        viewView: { class: 'foam.u2.detail.TabbedDetailView', hideActions: true }
      })
    .end()
    .start('div').style({ flex: 1, position: 'relative', overflow: 'hidden' })
      .start('p').addClass('p-semiBold').add('SectionedDetailView').end()
      .tag({
        class: 'foam.comics.v3.DetailView',
        data: rec,
        config: config,
        viewView: { class: 'foam.u2.detail.SectionedDetailView' }
      })
    .end()
  .end();
});

value.markdown:
### Overriding CRUD Actions (ComicsAction)

`foam.comics.v3.ComicsAction` extends `foam.lang.Action` with two extra slots:
- `internalIsEnabled(config, data, ...)` — internal method for permission/availability check before the base `isEnabled`
- `internalIsAvailable(config, controllerMode, data, ...)` — same for visibility
WARN: Do not override these two methods in your custom action definition, these are used by the detail view to maintain a default behaviour, define your COMICS actions as any other action.

To override a default CRUD action, declare a `ComicsAction` with the same `name` as the action you want to replace (`edit`, `save`, `delete`, `copy`) as an action on the model. `DetailView.getActionsOverrides()` finds it and merges it.

```javascript
foam.CLASS({
  name: 'MyModel',
  actions: [
    {
        class: 'foam.comics.v3.ComicsAction',
        name: 'edit',
        isEnabled: function(...) {
            // Some custom is enabled check
        }
    }
  ]
});
```

#### Adding Custom Actions

Any regular `foam.lang.Action` on the model (not a ComicsAction) is rendered in the trailing action bar when in VIEW mode:

```javascript
actions: [{
  name: 'archive',
  label: 'Archive',
  isAvailable: function(active) { return active; },
  code: function() {
    this.active = false;
    // Note: this sets it on data but won't save without a DAO put
  }
}]
```

value.code:
// DemoContactV2: ComicsAction to hide delete for active contacts +
// a regular Action that appears in the trailing bar
foam.CLASS({
  package: 'foam.u2.demos',
  name: 'DemoContactV2',
  extends: 'foam.u2.demos.DemoContact',

  actions: [
    {
       class: 'foam.comics.v3.ComicsAction',
       name: 'delete',
       isAvailable: function(active) {
          return ! active;
       }
    },
    {
      name: 'deactivate',
      label: 'Deactivate',
      isAvailable: function(active) { return active; },
      code: function() {
        this.active = false;
      }
    }
  ]
});

// Create a DAO of DemoContactV2
var dao2 = foam.dao.EasyDAO.create({
  of: foam.u2.demos.DemoContactV2,
  seqNo: true,
  daoType: 'MDAO'
});
var DC2 = foam.u2.demos.DemoContactV2;
[
  { name: 'Alice Chen',  contactType: 'BUSINESS', organization: 'Acme', active: true  },
  { name: 'Carol White', contactType: 'BUSINESS', organization: 'Globex', active: false }
].forEach(function(d) { dao2.put(DC2.create(d)); });

// Click Alice (active) — no Delete in overflow, Deactivate in action bar
// Click Carol (inactive) — Delete appears in overflow
start('div').style({ height: '500px', position: 'relative', overflow: 'hidden' })
  .tag({
    class: 'foam.comics.v3.DAOController',
    data: dao2
  })
.end();

value.markdown:
### viewBorder

`config.viewBorder` wraps the entire detail form. Default is `NullBorder` (no wrapping). Common options:

```javascript
// No border (default):
viewBorder: { class: 'foam.u2.borders.NullBorder' }

// Card border — adds shadow and rounded corners:
viewBorder: { class: 'foam.u2.borders.CardBorder' }

// Background card — adds background colour:
viewBorder: {
  class: 'foam.u2.borders.BackgroundCard',
  backgroundColor: '$grey50'
}
```

The browse view's border is controlled separately by `browseBorder` (defaults to `CardBorder`).

#### finished Topic

`DetailView` publishes a `finished` topic after a successful SAVE or DELETE. `DAOController` listens to it and reloads the data from the DAO, keeping the detail view in sync after external changes.

You can subscribe to `finished` in custom code:

```javascript
var dv = this.DetailView.create({ ... });
dv.finished.sub(function() {
  console.log('Record was saved or deleted');
});
```

value.code:
groupDAO = x.groupDAO;
grantDAO = x.grantDAO;

async function convertGroup(g) {
  let ps = (await g.permissions.dao.select()).array;
  log(g.id, g.parent, ps);

  let ag = foam.core.grant.GrantAssignment.create({
    id: 'group-' + g.id,
    name: 'Group ' + g.id,
    grant: foam.core.grant.CompoundGrant.create({
      grants: ps.map(p => {
        if ( p.id.startsWith('@') ) return foam.core.grant.SharedGrant.create({grantId: p.id.substring(1)});
        return foam.core.grant.PermissionGrant.create({permission: p.id});
      })
    })
  });
  if ( g.parent ) ag.grant.grants.push(foam.core.grant.SharedGrant.create('group-' + g.parent));
  log(foam.json.stringify(ag));
  // grantDAO.put(ag);
}

groups = (await groupDAO.select()).array;
groups.forEach(async g => {
  convertGroup(g);
});

// Read the DAO once. Whatever this returns is the block's value.
var rs = await regions.filteredDAO.select();
return rs.array.filter(r => r.countryId === 'CA');

// A function reading another function: canadaRows ran to completion
// before this block started.
return canadaRows.length;

// Returning a DAO makes the block usable wherever a DAO is. A block whose
// name ends in DAO is bound without the suffix too, so canada works as well.
var dao = foam.dao.MDAO.create({ of: foam.core.auth.Region }, x);
canadaRows.forEach(r => dao.put(r));
return dao;

// Reads the DAO the block above returned.
var s = await canadaDAO.select();
return s.array.length;

value.markdown:
# Ordering

The optional `orderBy` parameter controls sort order. Uses the same `__Property__` descriptor format as Sinks.

## Single field ascending

```json
{"class":"__Property__","forClass_":"foam.core.auth.Region","name":"code"}
```

## Single field descending

```json
{"class":"foam.mlang.order.Desc","arg1":{"class":"__Property__","forClass_":"foam.core.auth.Region","name":"code"}}
```

## Two fields

```json
{
  "class":"foam.mlang.order.ThenBy",
  "head":{"class":"__Property__","forClass_":"foam.core.auth.Region","name":"countryId"},
  "tail":{"class":"__Property__","forClass_":"foam.core.auth.Region","name":"code"}
}
```

## Three fields, last one descending

`ThenBy` is a binary combinator — nest it to chain more than two fields:
```json
{
  "class":"foam.mlang.order.ThenBy",
  "head":{
    "class":"foam.mlang.order.ThenBy",
    "head":{"class":"__Property__","forClass_":"foam.core.auth.Region","name":"countryId"},
    "tail":{"class":"__Property__","forClass_":"foam.core.auth.Region","name":"code"}
  },
  "tail":{"class":"foam.mlang.order.Desc","arg1":{"class":"__Property__","forClass_":"foam.core.auth.Region","name":"isoCode"}}
}
```

