### Validation

`PropertyBorder` automatically shows the error returned by `validateObj` or `internalValidateObj`. The error appears in the default text color when the field is empty, and switches to destructive color once the user has entered a value. Read the validation doc for more details on validating properties and objs. 

If a property has a default value (usually empty string or 0 or undefined), the property border renders the error as a muted string under the input field, however when the user inputs an invalid value the PropertyBorder adjusts to display the error in red as well as a red border around the field.

```javascript
// In model definition with no extra PropertyBorder config needed:
{
  class: 'String',
  name: 'name',
  required: true,
  minLength: 3
}
```

value.code:
var DC = foam.u2.demos.DemoContact;
// Empty contact — NAME has required: true that returns 'Required.'
// The error will show in default color; type one char to see the error change colours and then disappear once the value is valid
var empty = DC.create();
start().startContext({ data: empty }).add(DC.NAME.__).endContext().end();

