### Reactive labelFormatter

`labelFormatter` is called **once** at render time (`this` = Element, `data` = model instance). To make the label react to property changes, map over a slot:

```javascript
{
  name: 'organization',
  labelFormatter: function(data) {
    // data.contactType$map() is a slot
    this.add(data.contactType$.map(function(contactType) {
      return contactType === 'BUSINESS' ? 'Organization Name' : 'Employer';
    }));
  }
}
```

Toggle **Contact Type** in the example below and watch the Organization label update live — without any re-render of the whole form.

